\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Forth rode the knights of old
\par With armour gleaming bright,
\par By noble deeds and actions bold
\par To fight for God and right,
\par To lay the tyrant low,
\par To set the captive free,
\par The hosts of evil to o'erthrow
\par By might of purity.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. A vision flamed above,
\par A voice within spoke clear,
\par The symbol of Christ's mighty love
\par Shown radiant and near.
\par Then, burning with desire,
\par By zeal and love possessed,
\par The knights of old with heart afire
\par Rode out upon the quest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. In every age the same,
\par From hut and princely hall,
\par The pilgrim knights who bear His name
\par Have followed at His call.
\par Now each with glory crowned,
\par And waiting on His will,
\par They stand His splendid throne around
\par And serve more nobly still.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Still, still the vision glows,
\par Still calls the voice divine;
\par Still sink the weak, oppressed by foes,
\par And still the captives pine;
\par Still loyal to their Lord,
\par With zeal and patience shod,
\par With shield of faith and mystic sword,
\par Go forth the knights of God.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

